   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 4. Structure of the contamination: depth layers, universal combinations, and the mechanism\n- **Layers.** Per contaminated state, compute the rank over all 25 $t$ of $\\{\\hat k_B(t)\\}$. Then $n_L-\\text{rank}$ is the number of **$t$-independent** clean combinations for that state, and `nullT` gives them exactly (rationalized).\n- **Universal combinations.** $v$ is a universal combination for a set of states if it lies in the common null space. Its signal $v\\cdot\\hat s$ is checked too.\n- **Mechanism test.** Is $\\hat k_B$ in the span of the signal directions $\\hat s_C$ of the HW states $C$ above $B$ (dominance, $C\\neq$ top)? This is only a real test when those signals do not already span everything.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "lg[x_] := If[x == 0, -99, Round[Log10[x], 1]];\nkStack[sts_] := Flatten[Table[Table[d[μc][[1 ;; nL]], {d, data}], {μc, sts}], 1];\nrankT[sts_] := With[{s = SingularValueList[N[kStack[sts], 40], Tolerance -> 0]}, Count[s/Max[s], x_ /; x > 10^-15]];\nnullT[sts_] := With[{m = N[kStack[sts], 40]}, With[{sv = SingularValueList[m, Tolerance -> 0], V = SingularValueDecomposition[m][[3]]}, With[{r = Count[sv/Max[sv], x_ /; x > 10^-15]},\n     Map[Rationalize[Chop[#/#[[Ordering[Abs[#], -1][[1]]]], 10^-20], 10^-15] &, Transpose[V][[r + 1 ;;]]]]]];\ncontam = Select[nonTop, ! cleanQ[#] &];\nlayer1 = Select[contam, rankT[{#}] <= 2 && Max[Abs[Flatten[Table[{d[#][[2]] - 16 d[#][[1]], d[#][[3]] - 72 d[#][[1]]}, {d, data}]]]] < 10^-15 &];\nv2 = {72, -9, 1, 0};\naboveQ[c_, b_] := c =!= b && c[[1]] >= b[[1]] && c[[1]] + c[[2]] >= b[[1]] + b[[2]];\nspanRes[k_, S_] := If[S === {}, 1, With[{Q = Orthogonalize[S]}, Norm[k - Total[(Conjugate[#] . k) # & /@ Q]]/Norm[k]]];\nlayerTab = Table[Module[{above = Select[nonTop, aboveQ[#[[1]], μc[[1]]] &]},\n    {μc, rankT[{μc}], nullT[{μc}],\n     lg[Max[Table[Abs[v2 . d[μc][[1 ;; nL]]]/Max[Abs[d[μc][[1 ;; nL]]]], {d, data}]]], lg[Min[Table[Abs[v2 . d[μc][[nL + 1 ;; 2 nL]]], {d, data}]]],\n     MatrixRank[N[Table[data[[1]][c][[nL + 1 ;; 2 nL]], {c, above}], 30], Tolerance -> 10^-15],\n     lg[Max[Table[spanRes[N[d[μc][[1 ;; nL]], 60], Select[N[Table[d[c][[nL + 1 ;; 2 nL]], {c, above}], 60], Norm[#] > 10^-20 &]], {d, data}]]]}], {μc, contam}];\nColumn[{Grid[Join[{{\"contaminated state\", \"rank of k-hat(t)\", \"t-independent clean combinations (exact)\", \"log10 |v2·k-hat|\", \"log10 |v2·s-hat| (min over t)\", \"rank of signals above\", \"log10 dist(k-hat, span of signals above)\"}}, layerTab], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n  Grid[{{\"layer-1 states (k22 = 16 k11, k33 = 72 k11 exactly)\", layer1}, {\"common t-independent null space of layer 1\", nullT[layer1]}, {\"common null space of [5,5,0], [5,4,1]x2, [5,3,2]\", nullT[Select[contam, Not[MemberQ[layer1, #]] && # =!= {{4, 4, 2}, 1} &]]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
