   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result for $[4,1,0]^2$ (2026-10-02; 250 digits, $\\varepsilon_0=10^{-8}$, extrapolation error $\\le10^{-23}$; data 1059 s)\n**Every quantity has a closed form.** All ratFit searches succeeded: total degree $\\le9$, held-out validation $\\le10^{-18}$, except the $A$-part of $\\hat k_{11}$ on $[5,4,1]$ (degree 9, $2\\times10^{-15}$, marginal). Insertions $d_{(1,1)},d_{(2,2)},d_{(3,3)},d_{(4,3)}$, $h=1$, $t=\\theta_{12}$, with $\\hat k$ normalized to $\\hat k_{(4,3)}=1$.\n- **Already clean:** $[8,1,1]$, $[7,3,0]$, $[7,2,1]_{1,2}$.\n- **Layer 1:** $[6,4,0]$, $[6,3,1]_{1,2}$, $[6,2,2]$. Exactly $\\hat k_{22}=16\\hat k_{11}$ and $\\hat k_{33}=72\\hat k_{11}$ at every $t$ and for both copies.\n  - $[6,4,0]$: $\\hat k=(-\\tfrac1{72},-\\tfrac29,-1,1)$, constant in $t$.\n  - $[6,2,2]$: $\\hat k_{11}=-\\dfrac{7t-23}{360(2t-7)}$.\n  - $[6,3,1]_c$: $\\hat k_{11,c}=-\\dfrac{(189t^2-767t+445)+\\sigma_c(7t-26)\\sqrt{25+24t^2}}{360\\,(49t^2-182t+75)}$, with $\\sigma_c=\\pm1$ ($D=4(25+24t^2)$).\n  - So $16d_{11}-d_{22}$ and $72d_{11}-d_{33}$ are $t$- and copy-independent clean combinations on layer 1.\n- **Layer 2:** $[5,5,0]$, $[5,4,1]_{1,2}$, $[5,3,2]$. Their common $t$-independent null space is exactly\n  $$v_2=72\\,d_{(1,1)}-9\\,d_{(2,2)}+d_{(3,3)}.$$\n  $v_2$ is clean with nonzero signal on all four of them. It has zero signal on layers 0 and 1 (it annihilates their signal patterns), and it is useless on the bottom irrep.\n- **Bottom irrep $[4,4,2]$:** $\\hat k$ spans all 4 directions over $t$, so its clean combination is genuinely $t$-dependent:\n  $$\\hat k=\\Big(-\\tfrac{(t-1)(t-2)(2t-7)}{18P},\\;-\\tfrac{2(t-1)^2(8t-19)}{9P},\\;-\\tfrac{2(t-1)(4t^2-5t+9)}{P},\\;1\\Big),\\quad P=11t^3+61t-90,\\quad\\rho=\\tfrac{P}{90}.$$\n  Compare $[3,1,0]$'s bottom irrep $[3,3,2]$, with $\\rho=(7t^2-12)/20$, and the adjoint singlet, with $\\rho=(2t-3)/3$.\n- **Multiplicity discriminants:** $D_{[7,2,1]}=\\tfrac94(100+21t^2)$, $D_{[6,3,1]}=4(25+24t^2)$, $D_{[5,4,1]}=\\tfrac{25}{4}(4+21t^2)$. In $[3,1,0]$ they were $\\tfrac14(256+105t^2)$ and $16(1+3t^2)$. Every copy-dependent quantity is $P(t)+Q(t)\\,\\sigma_c\\sqrt{D}$, i.e. linear in the copy's transfer eigenvalue.\n- **Mechanism, partially tested.** The contamination direction of $B$ lies in the span of the signal directions of the HW states above $B$. This holds exactly ($10^{-25}$) in the two cases where the test is non-trivial: $[6,4,0]$ against $[7,3,0]$, and $[5,5,0]$ against $[7,3,0],[6,4,0]$. Elsewhere the higher signals already span everything, so those cases test nothing. This is why the $t$-independent combinations are exactly those that annihilate the signal patterns of the shallower layers. *Conjecture, not yet proven:* the clean space of $B$ is the annihilator of $\\mathrm{span}\\{\\hat s_C: C\\text{ above }B\\}$ intersected with the minimal relevant set.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
